ontology soil
	version 1.0
	using imod, physical, earth
	in domain imod:Soil;

/**
 * # Soil material and its observations
 *
 * SoilBody identifies a bounded material body of mineral or organic soil.
 * Soil properties and the stated delineation convention establish its extent.
 * The material may include water and air in its pores. A soil profile describes
 * vertical variation through that material; a map unit or classification names
 * a descriptive grouping rather than the particular body being observed.
 *
 * This is a material description, distinct from descriptions of organisms and
 * communities living in soil. It does not attribute agency to the soil body or
 * retype living individuals as material Subjects. A portion selected for sampling
 * represents the larger body only under an appropriate observation model.
 *
 * This reading follows the [NRCS account of soil as a natural body](https://www.nrcs.usda.gov/resources/education-and-teaching-materials/soil-facts).
 */
thing SoilBody
    "An individuated body of mineral or organic soil material."
    is physical:MaterialBody;

/**
 * ## Soil bulk density
 *
 * BulkDensity compares dry soil mass with the bulk volume occupied by the same
 * soil body, including pore space. Particle density instead uses the volume of
 * the solid particles. The two measurements describe different quantities even
 * when derived from material taken at the same site.
 *
 * The observation states the moisture condition used for the bulk volume, the
 * soil fraction included, and the drying basis for the mass. Wet-mass bulk
 * density is a different measurement convention from this dry-mass quantity.
 * The mass and volume represent the same soil fraction and sampling support.
 * A representative core can supply evidence for that observation; it is not
 * the definition of the whole soil body. Heterogeneous bodies require an explicit
 * sampling support.
 * Bulk density alone does not establish a compaction history or soil suitability.
 *
 * The measurement meaning follows [NRCS bulk-density guidance](https://www.nrcs.usda.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/Soil%20Bulk%20Density%20Moisture%20Aeration.pdf).
 */
quality BulkDensity
    "Dry soil mass per bulk volume of a soil body, including pore space, at a stated moisture condition."
    is imod:Ratio of soil:SoilBody
    describes soil:SoilBody;

/**
 * ## Soil aggregates and their size
 *
 * SoilAggregate identifies a cluster whose particles are held together as a
 * recognizable material unit. An aggregate and an individual mineral or rock
 * grain have different criteria for unity. A loose collection selected by a
 * particle-size interval does not by itself establish an aggregate.
 *
 * AggregateDiameter describes the aggregate at its observed preparation and
 * moisture state. Measuring intact aggregates and measuring grains after
 * dispersion answer different questions. An aggregate-size distribution must
 * therefore be distinguished from a primary-particle size distribution.
 *
 * Texture describes the relative sizes of the selected soil particles under a
 * stated convention. Aggregation describes their organization. Neither one
 * alone determines erosion, infiltration or soil retention; observations and
 * models establish their contributions in the particular setting.
 *
 * This distinction follows [NRCS soil structure](https://www.nrcs.usda.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/Soil%20Structure%20and%20Macropores.pdf)
 * and [aggregate stability](https://www.nrcs.usda.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/nrcs142p2_051276.pdf).
 */
thing SoilAggregate
    "An individuated cluster of soil particles with stronger internal cohesion than its contacts with neighboring particles."
    is physical:MaterialBody;

quality AggregateDiameter
    "Diameter assigned to a soil aggregate under a stated geometric or equivalent-size convention and preparation state."
    is imod:Length of soil:SoilAggregate
    describes soil:SoilAggregate;

/**
 * ## Soil compression and leaching
 *
 * SoilCompaction compresses a soil material volume and reduces its bulk pore
 * space. SoilLeaching carries dissolved constituents out of an identified soil
 * volume with moving water. A soil profile, the material it describes and a soil
 * classification are different observational targets.
 *
 * Compaction is a process, while calling soil compacted requires a stated
 * comparison. Neither a measured density alone nor a missing measurement proves
 * an episode of compaction. Leaching does not imply that all solute has left the
 * soil or establish its eventual destination. Models describe loading, water
 * movement and constituent transfer at the support of the observation.
 */
process SoilCompaction
    "Mechanical compression of soil that reduces its bulk pore space.";

process SoilLeaching
    "Transport of dissolved constituents out of an identified soil volume by water moving through it.";
